# Build and tool artefacts
/composer.phar
/vendor/bin/
/node_modules/

# Dev-only composer packages inside the tracked `vendor/`.
#
# `vendor/` is committed and shipped, because wordpress.org never runs
# `composer install` and the plugin would otherwise load no dependencies at all. That
# makes an ordinary `composer install` dangerous: it drops phpcs, wpcs,
# phpcompatibility, parallel-lint and the phpcodesniffer installer into a directory
# that gets committed and zipped. That is several MB of tooling no site owner needs,
# and it tells anyone reading the ZIP exactly which linters the project uses.
#
# They stay in `composer.lock` and in `require-dev` - CI installs them itself. Only the
# copy inside `vendor/` is unwanted. Install with `composer install --no-dev` when
# the runtime tree is what you are changing.
#
# ⚠ `dealerdirect/phpcodesniffer-composer-installer` is a Composer *plugin*, not a
# linter, and it has to be allowed in `config.allow-plugins` for `composer install` to
# succeed at all. Removing it from the tree is safe; removing it from `composer.json`
# is what broke the install.
/vendor/dealerdirect/
/vendor/php-parallel-lint/
/vendor/phpcompatibility/
/vendor/phpcsstandards/
/vendor/squizlabs/
/vendor/wp-coding-standards/

# Editor and OS noise.
#
# The previous 130-line gitignore.io template listed individual .idea/ files
# (workspace.xml, tasks.xml, shel/, тАж) and so let the rest of the directory тАФ
# deployment.xml, modules.xml, inspectionProfiles/ тАФ sit in `git status` as
# untracked. Ignoring the whole directory is both shorter and the only thing
# that actually works. Nothing in here is part of the plugin.
/.idea/
/.vscode/
/*.sublime-workspace
/desktop.ini
/Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Working material, not source.
#
# `plans/` is the release plan and `docs/` the generated hook catalogue and the
# HPOS audit. Both are useful to keep on disk and neither belongs in the
# repository; `docs/` is excluded from the release ZIP as well, which is
# deliberate тАФ the catalogue ships with the extension contract once that
# milestone is cut.
/plans/
/docs/

# The real-WordPress integration harness.
#
# Not part of the plugin and not part of the repository, but it stays on disk
# because it is the only thing here that can catch a defect reading cannot: it
# found a credential-encryption path that was non-functional in production while
# every unit test was green. It is gitignored rather than deleted so that the next
# change can still be run against a real database instead of only linted.
/tests/

# /tools/ is working material and stays out of the repository - with one exception.
#
# `make-pot.php` regenerates assets/languages/wsklad.pot, and the .pot ships in the
# release ZIP. A shipped artefact that cannot be rebuilt from the repository is one
# nobody can keep in step with the code, and this one had already drifted: ten msgids
# for screens deleted months ago, and a Russian entry that never resolved because the
# msgid used a hyphen where the source used an em dash.
#
# So the generator is tracked. It has no dependencies beyond PHP on purpose - it runs
# in CI, where `composer install --no-dev` leaves no autoloader to lean on.
# `composer i18n:pot` writes the template, `composer i18n:pot:check` is the CI gate,
# and .distignore keeps the whole directory out of the ZIP.
/tools/*
!/tools/make-pot.php
